  "seoDescription": "Soils have moulded humans. And humans have shaped soils by ploughing through a natural endowment of fertile dirt. In “Dirt: The Erosion of Civilization” (2012), David Montgomery, Professor of Earth and Space Sciences at the University of Washington, traces the use and abuse of soil in Mesopotamia, Ancient Greece, the Roman Empire, China, European colonialism,"
