  "seoDescription": "As rivers run dry, and glaciers melt into torrents, viruses shuttered in the ice, in lakebeds and in soils beneath Arctic ice are released after eternities of containment. Mapping the tree diagrams of these primeval viruses against the genealogies of possible hosts allow scientists at the University of Toronto to forecast possible viral spillovers. Greta"
